* text=auto eol=lf

*.parquet binary
*.csv.gz binary
*.csv text eol=lf

# The raw ANAC fixtures are cut byte for byte from the published monthly
# files and exist to prove the measured layout (latin-1, CRLF for
# 2000-2009, LF from 2010) against `src/airline_delays/ingest/layouts.py`'s declaration. `-text`
# disables EOL normalisation entirely, in both directions: without it the
# `*.csv` rule above rewrote the 2002 sample's CRLF to LF on checkout and
# `tests/test_ingest.py` failed on every fresh clone. Do not fold these back
# into the `*.csv` rule -- `tests/test_ingest.py::TestFixtureBytes` fails
# loudly, naming this file, if they are.
tests/fixtures/vra_raw_sample_*.csv -text

# Deterministic script output -- GitHub should not compute language stats
# nor a "human" diff over these. data/analysis/*.parquet and *.csv.gz are
# tracked since DECISIONS.md ADR-0014; the blanket `*.parquet`/`*.csv.gz`
# binary rule above already covers them, and this just marks them generated
# too, the same way data/derived/ already is.
data/derived/** linguist-generated
data/analysis/*.parquet linguist-generated
data/analysis/*.csv.gz linguist-generated
docs/dictionary.md linguist-generated
reports/summary.json linguist-generated
# reports/theory/figures/*.svg are drawn by theory/figures.py from fixed
# geometry (`just theory`); the diff a reviewer wants is the Python, not the XML.
reports/theory/figures/*.svg linguist-generated

# data/external/*.csv is NOT marked linguist-generated, on purpose: it is
# human judgment (the node map, each merger's date, each code's class), and
# its diff is exactly what needs to stay reviewable in a pull request.
